WEBVTT

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:05.680
Everyone, when you're watching Deltora Quest,

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.100
Make sure you're in a well- lit room and sit far away from the TV!

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:23.970
When I open this door
Kono doa akereba atarashii sekai ga

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.860
A brand new world is starting right now
Ima hajimarunda

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:34.440
Even if there are painful things on my way
Tsurai koto ga aru toshitemo

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:40.840
I will show you that I can overcome them all
Kitto norikoetemiseru

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:48.600
I'm starting to walk on a brand new world now
Atarashii sekai ni ima arukidashita soko ha

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:54.830
And I'm sure there are [Dreams] and [Hope] there
[Yume] ya [Kibou] ga aru kara

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:58.050
This feeling is making my heart beat so fast
Dokidoki suru kono kimochi

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.180
And there's no one who can stop it
darenimo tomerarenai

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:06.200
My heart is tightening and jumping all over the place
Kyun to hazumu kokoro

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:10.560
So start flapping your wings from now
Koko kara habataiteiku

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.610
and soar high to the sky up there
ano sora he to takaku

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:19.580
Aiming for [Tomorrow] and [The Future] beyond
[Ashita] [Mirai] mezashite

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:22.910
We will definitely grow bigger someday
Itsuka ookiku nareru to

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:26.180
That's what I believed
sou shinjiteiru no

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:31.340
That's why, just spread your wings
Dakara tsubasa wo hiroge

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:54.750
The Japanese Deltora Quest is brought to you in English by ToranSubs

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:57.500
<i>My name is Lief.</i>

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:04.070
<i>In order to bring peace back to Deltora, I defeated evil monsters and recovered the topaz, ruby and opal!</i>

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:07.090
<i>Honestly... You're always just being reckless though.</i>

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:07.840
<i>Jasmine!</i>

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.040
<i>It's all thanks to me that you even got this far.</i>

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:11.600
<i>And don't forget about me either.</i>

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:12.500
<i>Barda!</i>

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:15.600
<i>Filli! Kree!</i>

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:20.200
<i>We are in the middle of our journey to search for the seven gems!</i>

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.750
<i>And right now, we're on our way to the
Shifting Sands where the fourth gem is hidden!</i>

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:36.200
Lief!

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.500
Have some; they're good.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.700
The apple tree over there was complaining,

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:55.150
Saying "these are so heavy, hurry and take them".

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:56.000
Thieves!

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:01.320
You dirty thieves! Give my apples back!

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.900
Give my apples back!!

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:07.900
They're this old woman's apples...?

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:09.800
Seems like it.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.140
Those are my apples, aren't they?! Give them back!!

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.500
1, 2, 3...

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.440
Where are the rest?

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.900
Give them all back to me, right now!

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:26.900
How am I supposed to sell my products if you thieves have stolen my apples?!

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.040
You stole nine apples from me!

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.980
Where are the other three?!

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:34.700
We are really sorry about this, but I don't think we can return them to you.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:37.400
We already ate them, after all.

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:42.400
We're really sorry, but we were starving, so we just...

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:44.500
You ate them?!

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:57.810
I'm sure you dirty thieves thought that stealing from me would be easy because I'm 'just a weak old lady'.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:01.900
But unfortunately for you, my guards can move in an instant at a word's notice.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:05.220
Now, be punished for your sin, you dirty thieves!

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:06.510
Please wait...!

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:07.900
We'll trade them for these!

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:13.610
Why would you steal if you had this much?

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:14.400
Hold on!

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.500
You're taking all of it?

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.700
Isn't that way too expensive for just three apples?!

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:21.020
Be quiet!

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.230
You'd better not move.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:26.880
My guards really hate sudden movement, you see...

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:31.680
Even I have to be very careful and use smoke when harvesting their honey.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.870
You use smoke...?

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:37.390
Now, return to me, my little guards.

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:44.300
Take this as a lesson and don't commit such a shameless act again!

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.400
And here I thought that crossing the Broad River was scary...

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.100
Wh...What?

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:58.100
Now that I have a good look, you three seem to be travellers, am I right?

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:01.100
Good luck on your journey.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.500
Th-Thanks...

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.500
Now hurry up and get out of here!!

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:12.300
I see, Queen Bee Cider, huh...

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:15.610
Speaking of Queen Bee Cider,

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:19.510
I remember that I drank quite a lot of it back at Del Palace...

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:22.600
So it was made using these apples, huh...?

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.900
Keep going! It's one final dash until Rithmere!

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:33.100
Is it still far?

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.400
It's just a bit further.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.220
Aah, I'm so starved...

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.250
You can eat all you want when we get to Rithmere, my man!

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.300
Seems like they are all heading to this Rithmere place...

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:48.830
Rithmere? Isn't that the town just before the Shifting Sands, where the next gem is?

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:51.200
I'm glad that there's a town nearby.

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:52.550
Why?

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:57.590
We can blend in with the townspeople, as well as make some money.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:58.400
Make money?

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:01.760
We can't exactly continue our journey with no money, right?

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:06.630
Ladies and Gentlemen! Don't you want to make some money before getting to Rithmere?

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.800
-Some money?
Some money?

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.340
No matter where you come from, my bird and I here are going to share some fortune with all of you!

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:10.400
What's this, I wonder...?

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:14.810
No matter where you come from, my bird and I here are going to share some fortune with all of you!

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:17.000
Bird...?

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:20.200
Little missy!

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:23.740
Seeing as you have a bird of your own as well,

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:26.300
How about we play a little game?

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.890
I'm not interested in games.

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:31.340
Besides, I don't have the money to play.

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:33.220
This is all I have left.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.910
One silver coin is more than enough, Missy!

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:39.510
Come, test your luck here!

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:40.900
Test my luck...?

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:46.200
Yes! If you're lucky enough, that silver coin of yours could be multiplied by five or even ten!

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.490
Ten times?!

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:53.050
It's just a simple game where my bird will spin this board.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:58.210
Guess where will it stop correctly, and your money will be multiplied by the number where it stopped!

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:02.450
However! If it lands on the bird, you will only win this little carving.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:09.010
Now, now, Ladies and Gentlemen! Will you be able to "Beat the Bird"?

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:10.880
A bird?

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:13.120
So the one spinning the board is the bird?

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:15.720
If I were playing, I'd probably bet on 4.

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:22.490
I've been had! That's four silver coins!

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:26.130
If you had bet your money just now, I would have completely lost...!

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.620
Amazing, Jasmine!

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:33.280
However, why stop at quadruple?

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:37.740
After all, you might even multiply it by five, six, no, even ten times if you're lucky enough!

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:41.240
Alright, I'll go bet some!

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:41.330
Give me the 5!
Alright, I'll go bet some!

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:42.180
Give me the 5!

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:43.200
I'm getting the 10!

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:45.600
Let's give it a try too, Barda!

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:47.950
Sure, here.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:54.600
Well, we can't fill our stomachs with one silver coin anyway.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:59.300
You guys won again!

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:03.800
Hey, spin it properly will you? Are you trying to make me broke?

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:07.870
Shall we give it a shot?

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:09.200
What number will you bet?

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.000
Let's wait and see for now.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:13.500
Are you hungry?

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:16.700
Wait a bit, okay? We're trying to get some money now.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:22.490
The wheel of fortune goes round and round...

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:27.810
Again?! I lost again?! Save me!!

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:38.490
Oh? Too bad!

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.610
You won this cute little bird carving this time.

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:47.870
Come on, land on the 10s this time!

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:51.530
Alright, I'm betting on the 10s too!

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:56.580
The wheel of fortune goes round and round, where it will stop, no one knows...

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:13.800
The wheel of fortune keeps spinning round and round...

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:20.130
Oh, this is unusual! The bird won twice in a row!

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:23.720
Seems like we lost, huh...

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:25.610
Too bad about your loss...

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:28.270
Here, little missy, a cute little bird.

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:31.650
Let's just look for some work.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:32.810
Guess you're right.

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:36.610
Now, Ladies and Gentlemen! It's your final chance before I close my shop!

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:39.810
Close the shop?! Damn, I'd better get back my loss this time!

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:42.410
Fine, I'll bet everything on this final chance!

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.100
Filli?

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:51.790
Alright, your last chance! Round and round it goes...!

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:56.980
Filli!

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:07.680
Look, he cheated!!

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:12.000
Then, does it mean that that bastard was able to control the board as he pleased?!

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:14.870
What's "Beat the Bird" about this?! Grab him!!

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:15.690
Get him!

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:17.230
Have mercy!

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.510
So it was all a ruse?!

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.100
Just let it go.

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:31.820
Okay...

00:10:58.260 --> 00:10:59.990
This place sure is lively.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:01.490
It's like a festival!

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:28.500
Some teeth he's got...

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:30.300
Talk about creepy...

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:36.980
Should we look for work first? Or perhaps, some food first?

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:39.500
Food comes first, of course. Isn't that obvious?

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.000
But we really are broke, you know?

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:45.340
Then what about that?

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:51.850
'This way to Champion Inn...'

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:58.210
'The official inn for the Games, bed and board, amazing prices,' it says.

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:00.100
Whether or not it's cheap is meaningless.

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:01.800
We're penniless after all.

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:04.310
Not that; the one next to it.

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:08.770
'The Rithmere Games.'

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:13.510
'Come one, come all. Test your strength and skill. Every finalist will receive...'

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:14.930
100 gold coins?!

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:18.400
And the winner gets... 1000 gold coins?!!

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:21.370
We'll get 100 gold coins just by surviving the preliminaries!

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:23.900
That means we can eat anything we want, right?!

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:26.370
Then what are we waiting for?!

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:29.310
You're not going to participate in the Games, man?

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:35.570
Don't be stupid; it's more fun to just watch. We don't have any other entertainment after all.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:39.990
The Grey Guards won't even attack us during the Games too.

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:43.160
Seems like we made the right choice by stopping here.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:50.960
Perhaps even those Grey Guards would think it too tasteless to destroy something that everyone anticipates this much.

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:57.700
Win and get 1000 gold coins. Heck, even the 100 gold coins prize for surviving the prelims is enough!

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:05.900
Joanna... This year, we will definitely...

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:09.940
Stay until the main tournament!!

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:21.750
That's right, Orwen! You've gotten a lot stronger compared to last year after all!

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:25.200
Be careful not to break the other contestants like this rock, okay?

00:13:27.190 --> 00:13:28.600
What's with them...?

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:31.800
Showing off their strength or something, I would assume.

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:36.870
Besides, Lady Luck is definitely on the side of us spouses this year!

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:42.710
Damn straight! I heard that last year's champion went missing, didn't he?

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:45.850
1000 gold coins is a great deal after all.

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:50.160
Seems like most winners of the Games choose to stay here after they win.

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:51.710
Ow, ow, ow!!

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:53.000
Orwen...

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:57.620
Are you seriously going to let all of the people back in our village die?

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:00.690
They're starving right now, you know?

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:04.520
I know that.

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:10.960
If you seriously considered such a thing, then you would be better off being thrown into the Shifting Sands!

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.300
The Shifting Sands, huh...

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:16.840
The flier said Champion Inn, didn't it?

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.200
Yeah, it's here.

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:21.480
Alright. Let's go in.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:55.050
Welcome!

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:59.680
My name is Mother Brightly, the owner of this inn.

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:00.440
Um,

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:06.000
I just want to make sure, but all of you are
participating in the Rithmere Games, correct?

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:10.580
Well, we wanted to, but we don't really know how to register.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:15.240
My! My, my, my, my! Just leave the registering to me!

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:18.300
Actually, we're completely penniless at the moment.

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:21.340
Please let us work to pay for the room; we can even wash dishes.

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:24.900
There's no need for that! Now that you've come to this inn,

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:28.700
You three are proper participants in the Games, so you don't need to pay.

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:30.600
Really?

00:15:30.890 --> 00:15:32.500
Of course!

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:37.700
After all, if you keep winning until the main
tournament, you'll get some prize money, right?

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.050
You can just pay me back at that time.

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:41.500
I see!

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:46.700
And so that you can keep winning, I'm here to offer my services to you.

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:48.500
It's just that simple.

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:52.800
First, can you tell me your names and where you came from?

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:55.200
Ah, our names? I'm...

00:15:56.480 --> 00:16:00.420
My name is Berry, from Bushtown.

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:04.100
'Bushtown?' I've never heard of it before...

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:06.680
It's a small town to the north.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:08.580
These two are...

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:12.000
Birdie and Twig.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:15.600
They also come from Bushtown.

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:18.000
'From the same town', then...

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:22.200
Very well. Now, allow me lead the way.

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:25.000
Ah, but before that...

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:30.000
Please leave your weapons here.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.800
Weapons aren't allowed in this inn, you see.

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:34.490
Please understand.

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:46.400
You too, young lady.

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:52.900
What do you mean?

00:16:53.390 --> 00:16:55.770
Mother Brightly won't be fooled.

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:08.520
Next, we're going to have the physical examination. Just this way.

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:17.280
You three seem to be quite weakened from hunger...

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:21.400
But I'm sure you can put up a good fight when in top condition!

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:23.800
As for the last question...

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:25.800
What are your specialties?

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:34.300
Mine is tree climbing, I guess. I'm confident that I can cross a high place without losing my balance.

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:38.600
That's good. 'Birdie, specialty, nimbleness'.

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:41.140
So, what about you, Berry?

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:46.410
Just from looking at you, I would guess that you're a very strong man, am I right?

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:51.760
I knew it.

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:53.550
So, how about you, Twig?

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:55.910
Eh? Uhh, I'm...

00:17:56.290 --> 00:18:00.900
Speed, right? He's really fast on his feet, and he sure can jump high.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.600
I see, very well. Speed, then.

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:11.950
Nimbleness, strength and speed... I'd doubt anyone could beat you if you combined your strengths.

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:14.310
Alright then, please wait here for a moment.

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:23.800
Oh, and by the way...

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:26.800
Why did you call me Twig? It sounds so weak!

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:29.640
It's pretty cute though, Little Twig.

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:30.480
Jasmine!

00:18:30.820 --> 00:18:33.100
Do you really think we can use our real names here?

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:40.040
The rumours about us may have spread far and wide across Deltora, after all.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:49.910
Sorry for the wait!

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:59.100
These arm bands are your proof of participation. As long as you put them on, you can eat here for free and compete in the Rithmere Games!

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:06.100
Filli, it's almost time to eat.

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:11.500
Eat as much as you'd like and rest well.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:13.600
Here's the key to your room.

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:16.840
Excuse me, Mother Brightly...?

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:18.100
Yes?

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:22.400
What exactly are the Rithmere Games...?

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:28.500
It's a fighting tournament where the participants can go all out without worrying about injuries!

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:30.300
A fighting tournament?

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:36.600
That's right! Everyone really gives it their all, so it's a really exciting event.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:48.610
Geez, I'm so hungry...

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:03.670
So these are all entrants too, huh...

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:05.830
They sure look strong.

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:11.700
That guy is...

00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:31.400
Ah! That's my meat!!

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:44.640
Let's eat!

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:53.500
It's so nice to have proper meal after so long!

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:56.800
So, we're going to fight with all of the people here, then...

00:20:57.310 --> 00:20:59.770
It's a fighting tournament after all.

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:02.690
But we won't be able to continue our journey if we're injured...

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:05.300
Don't worry, I have a great plan.

00:21:05.600 --> 00:21:06.810
'Great plan?'

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:12.700
Basically, we can just cancel our registration after we finish eating.

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:19.510
Just tell her that we changed our minds. It can't be that uncommon, right? Besides, it's not like we're doing anything bad.

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:27.000
Mother Brightly!

00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:29.000
She's not here...?

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:31.820
Somehow, I have a bad feeling about this.

00:21:39.050 --> 00:21:40.500
Ah, over there.

00:21:41.280 --> 00:21:42.330
It's the exit.

00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:49.340
It's locked.

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:50.440
But why?

00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:55.910
There's no helping it. Let's go back to the hall; Mother Brightly is probably there too.

00:21:58.480 --> 00:22:02.900
Huh? What's this? I don't think I saw this when we arrived.

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:05.350
Mother Brightly!

00:22:09.310 --> 00:22:10.720
How strange...

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:13.400
Hey, look!

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:16.100
A lock?

00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:17.600
Don't tell me...

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:21.050
W-We're trapped here!?

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:27.420
Just what is happening here...?!

00:22:35.160 --> 00:22:40.390
Every moment is a gate to fantasia
Every moment is a gate to fantasia

00:22:41.040 --> 00:22:47.690
You just do it to be an shining star
You just do it to be an shining star

